      {
        "kind": "article",
        "label": "Article",
        "text": "Chandrayaan-3's lander Vikram touched down near the Moon's south pole on 23 August 2023, making India the first country to land in that region. Over the next ten days the Pragyan rover travelled about 100 metres and its laser spectroscope confirmed the presence of sulphur in the lunar soil.\n\nISRO has since said the lessons of the landing feed directly into Chandrayaan-4, a sample-return mission the Union Cabinet approved in September 2024. Engineers have reworked the lander's legs and its hazard-avoidance cameras for the heavier spacecraft.",
